WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.601
I, Joseph
Robinette Biden, Jr.,

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.670
do solemnly swear--

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.506
SPEAKER:
<i> Think about the challenge
 that Biden faces.</i>

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.876
<i> He's in adversarial
 relationships</i>

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:11.344
<i> from the start.</i>

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:15.181
SPEAKER 2:<i> December, we kept
 asking for the plan.</i>

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.248
There wasn't a plan.

00:00:16.815 --> 00:00:18.951
SPEAKER 3:
<i> Even in that moment
 of joy and renewal,</i>

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.087
people were extremely
conscious of...

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.123
<i> the inheritance we had.</i>

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.457
JEN PSAKI:
<i> We were playing catch up</i>

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.292
<i> from the moment
 the president took office.</i>

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.796
It was incredibly
challenging around here.

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:31.497
Don't tell Dr. Fauci

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.366
how many pieces of gum
I've swallowed.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.302
SPEAKER 4:<i> This is a period
 of remarkable division</i>

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.304
in the country.
Delta was raging.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.273
<i> Things were really
 falling apart.</i>

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.077
It's time to end
the forever war.

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.145
SPEAKER 5:<i> Biden's cabinet,
 not stupid people,</i>

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.813
and they got this
really wrong.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.250
SPEAKER 3:
<i> President Ghani said to me
 on the phone,</i>

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.885
<i> "I will stay and fight
 to the death."</i>

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.254
He fled the country
the next day.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.658
SPEAKER 6:<i> The United States
 has never seen</i>

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.061
<i> an adversary like this
 before.</i>

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.830
<i> We are in global struggle,</i>

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.264
and autocracy's on the rise.

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.199
Biden knew the moment
would come

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.602
<i> when you would need
 old alliances.</i>

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.472
That moment came
with Ukraine.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.974
SPEAKER 7:
<i> We began to pick up</i>

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.410
a massive Russian
military buildup.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.079
<i> So we go to Moscow quietly.</i>

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.216
I found President Putin
to be unapologetic,

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.751
<i> and his appetite for risk
 has grown.</i>

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.354
<i> I conveyed
 serious consequences</i>

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.191
that would flow from
military aggression.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.827
SPEAKER 8:
<i> The Biden administration</i>

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.263
<i> learned from the mistakes
 made in Afghanistan.</i>

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.799
<i> They responded by getting
 out ahead of events</i>

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.100
<i> instead
 of being behind them.</i>

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.602
JOE BIDEN:<i> We're living
 at an inflection point</i>

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.770
<i> in history.</i>

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.105
<i> We're engaged
 in a struggle</i>

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.107
<i> between democracy
 and autocracy.</i>

00:01:48.907 --> 00:01:51.343
<i> They're betting
 that democracy's days
 are numbered.</i>

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.346
♪ (DRAMATIC OUTRO MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

